WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.479
Hi, it's Michelle from Lab Muffin Beauty Science, chemistry PhD and skin care nerd yesterday

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.120
I was looking at my blog archives and I realized it's been

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.120
a little bit over a year since I last shared my evening skincare routine

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.639
I get a lot of questions on what products I've been using in my routine

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.320
And I usually just tell people to look at that post but I realize I haven't actually read that post in a while

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.480
So I thought it would be interesting to have a look at that and see what products I'm still using which products I've changed

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.919
and whether or not I still agree with the opinions of Michelle from

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.920
about 16 months ago

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.640
If you like nerding out about the science behind beauty products

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:42.799
make sure you click subscribe and click the notification bell so you don't miss any videos

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.960
So here's what I said in my post

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.640
"I don't like sharing my routine that often because I'm testing products and I don't want to endorse something that I haven't fully tested yet"

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.239
That is still the case. I still have to test lots of products and

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.960
yeah, I feel a little bit uncomfortable sharing it before I've really had a proper opinion

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.479
also when I share it a lot of people tend to ask me what I feel about that product and i'm usually not

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.959
quite ready yet. When i'm ready, I will post a review

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.200
"Secondly, it's because I think it's tempting for people to see my routine and try to copy it exactly. My skin's needs aren't the same as

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:18.399
another person's skin's needs, my budget and products that are available aren't the same as someone else"

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:22.239
I still completely agree with this. You need to know your own skin.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.159
Products that will work for me won't necessarily work for you

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.079
especially if you don't have the same skin type and skin conditions as I do.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.519
"In my opinion the most sensible route is to get to know your skin and its needs then base a routine on that

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.839
and your budget and product accessibility"

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:40.479
Yes completely still agree with that

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.720
You need to know your skin. You need to understand it and then

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.999
you can pick products without having to necessarily just base it on other people's recommendations.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:55.599
"That's why the Lab Muffin Guide to Basic Skincare starts with instructions on how to perform a skin assessment"

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:03.218
Yes doing a skin assessment is really important. You want to know what your skin is like - if it's dry, oily, sensitive dehydrated?

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:09.598
in the absence of whatever products you're using. A lot of people tend to use too many products and then their skin

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.360
might react to that. So yeah, a lot of people are using products that make their skin worse than

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.080
it might be if you use less products or even if you use no products at all

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.000
"You can't work out what your skin needs if you're using products that aren't right for your skin

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.359
then piling products suited to someone else's skin on top. You just can't"

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.520
Completely agree with that as well

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.559
So there's a third reason I don't really share my routine that often and

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.759
It's because I do get a lot of PR samples and like I said, I am usually testing some products

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.319
I think a lot of skincare instagrammers tend to share their routines and it'll be

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.719
like 10 products and half of them will change every single day

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:53.120
and I think that's kind of misleading to people. Skincare influencers should be people who know more about skin care or at least

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.559
are more immersed in that world and I think it gives people who are less experienced

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:03.839
a misleading idea of how many products should be in a routine and how often you should be changing them out

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:05.760
so I try not to do that

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.760
"I don't have an ETA for my next skincare eBook about advanced skincare routines and actives" - that is still the case.

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:15.279
I have started working on it. It is in progress, but

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:21.599
I don't know. I never know how long things take. So the next section is some general notes about my routine

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.920
They're more principles that guide me rather than strictly what's in my routine

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:31.839
"My routine isn't rigid. I adapt it based on how my skin feels" - that's still the case. I will pick products

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:37.759
based on whether my skin's feeling tight or dry, what the weather is like as well. "To adapt your routine effectively

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.759
you need to know how to assess your skin and know how your skin reacts to specific products

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.840
which is why I go on about one product at a time." Still the case

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.679
So here are the considerations for my personal routine that shape what I choose and these will be different for everyone

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.179
"My top priorities are anti-acne and anti-pigmentation"

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:58.399
That hasn't changed. I still get acne. I've actually had a really

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:06.560
nasty breakout here for a few weeks now. So yep, that's still going on. "I'm turning 32 this year." So young

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.200
"so i'm starting to see more white hairs and wrinkles"

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:15.680
I am seeing more white hairs. But since last time I don't think the wrinkles have really progressed, which is awesome

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.359
"My skin is oily and dehydration prone. I prefer not to layer too many products." Yep. Still the case

00:04:21.919 --> 00:04:27.839
"Too many steps gets confusing and heavy and increases the chances of the products interacting and clumping up or irritating my skin

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.000
and it takes longer than I can handle"

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.519
Still correct. "After cleansing, I like to use less than four products"

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:39.279
I think the average has actually gone down a bit since then. I think I generally use two or three

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.239
"I don't like things that are unpleasant to use even if they're more effective

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.379
I like to enjoy my skincare routine. I favor products with convenient packaging and easy application

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:50.319
over things that are a pain to use still true

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.880
I also like pleasant textures and scents"

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:59.040
Yes. "I don't have brand loyalty. I mix and match products from different brands all the time." That's definitely correct

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.840
"There are still products and brands that show up multiple times"

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:08.079
Yes, so I think part of this is brands that I tend to like more and have more um

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:14.179
reliable products but I think part of it is also just some brands have more products and more categories

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:17.359
and so I end up using more of their products as well

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.799
"Just because I don't regularly use a product i've loved in the past doesn't mean I no longer recommend it. Sometimes

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:27.600
products just fall by the wayside as a similar product has replaced it and I haven't felt the need to repurchase it.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.759
Sometimes I've switched to a different product and forgotten how good it was and then later on I rediscover it and go on a rave"

00:05:34.479 --> 00:05:36.719
I think that is going to happen in this video.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:43.919
So the next section is about cleansing. Last year I cleansed with an oil cleanser then a gentle foaming cleanser. "I shower at night

00:05:43.919 --> 00:05:46.639
so I step into the shower with oil cleanser on my face then

00:05:47.199 --> 00:05:54.079
step into the shower for the foaming cleanser." That's still pretty much my routine even during lockdown. "I use a lot of different cleansers

