So the Exfoliate and Smooth contains mostly glycolic acid and salicylic acid. The key things in step two are ascorbic acid

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.820
a few retinoids

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:38.159
ubiquinone, which is also known as coenzyme q10, vitamin e, resveratrol

00:16:38.399 --> 00:16:44.479
so two more antioxidants. I mostly use this when I'm staying at my boyfriend's house, which we're allowed to do in New South Wales.

00:16:44.639 --> 00:16:50.959
The neat thing about these is that with one of these I can do my face my back his face his back

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:56.479
and so I feel a lot less like I'm wasting the product because there is quite a lot of liquid in this.

00:16:56.639 --> 00:17:00.639
It actually says you're meant to massage the pad on your skin until it's dried out but

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.279
I don't think my skin really needs that much.

00:17:03.519 --> 00:17:07.859
So on exfoliant night, I tend to use one of those exfoliants and then follow up with moisturizer.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:11.199
So the third night last year was my vitamin c night

00:17:11.439 --> 00:17:16.979
It makes a huge difference to how quickly my acne marks fade. I used to pair this with 2% BHA

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:22.160
and I used a bunch of different L-ascorbic acid products depending on how irritated my skin was

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:28.959
On night three, I found that recently I haven't really been using vitamin c and I think that's because I haven't really had that much

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:35.520
post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation. So those are the brown marks that you have after your acne has faded away

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:40.640
I do have a breakout here, but it's not really at the stage where it's starting to become pigmented,

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.840
it's still trying to heal from the deep clogs.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:49.039
One of the things I've noticed about my vitamin C is that I've forgotten how long I've had it open for

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.999
which I think is just a beauty blogger issue

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:58.720
You get sent vitamin C products, you try them out, and then you put them aside and you can't remember when you opened it.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:03.999
So I tend to go for this sort of product which is anhydrous. That means it doesn't have water in it.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:10.000
This is paula's choice c25 super booster and it's like a gritty product where the

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:16.239
vitamin c is mixed in with a silicone. So with this sort of product because the vitamin c isn't with water

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:20.960
it doesn't decompose anywhere near as fast and so this one I haven't actually used in a while

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:27.839
but - not sure if you can see it - when you squeeze it out it is almost still entirely white,

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:34.000
well, it's a really pale beige color. If it was a water-based serum, this would be dark brown for sure by now.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.839
But because it's in the silicone base without any water, it's doing fine.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:42.400
So if you're someone who doesn't really use vitamin C that often I would recommend something like this.

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:49.919
The problem is sometimes if you put it on your skin, the gritty vitamin C doesn't really dissolve

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.760
that evenly and so you end up with little hot spots. It might get a bit itchy

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:59.839
and so when I use this, I mix it with some sort of hydrating toner so that it dissolves on your skin immediately

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:04.559
and you can spread it around. This is my favorite one, which is Jurlique's Activating Water Essence.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.959
This has been one of my favorites for ages

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:12.640
Um, it is quite expensive, but I find that it's really good at hydrating at a lot of different levels.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:17.539
You can get something similar with a cheaper product which just has glycerin

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:21.360
this has tons of different humectants and I find that that just lasts a bit longer.

00:19:21.679 --> 00:19:23.679
My skin is super dehydration prone though.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:30.400
Another vitamin c product that I've been using is Avene's A-Oxitive Serum. When I was originally filming, I was still testing this product.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.480
So I was testing it for a sponsored blog post

00:19:32.559 --> 00:19:36.159
(this video isn't sponsored) so I wasn't sure if it was going to stay in my routine

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:39.199
but it's been a few months now and I still use it once or twice a week

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:45.679
It contains a vitamin C derivative called ascorbyl glucoside and it gets around some of the problems with L-ascorbic acid

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:49.599
So it's very stable, and that means you don't have to worry if your product is going off

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:55.280
It's also stable on your skin, and that means you don't have to worry about staining so that fake tan looking

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:59.600
thing that stains your fingers and stains your skin and it has that metallic smell,

00:19:59.679 --> 00:20:03.679
so there's none of that. It can also be formulated at a higher pH and still work

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:08.799
which is really good because it means there's less irritation. With a lot of vitamin c derivatives

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:11.999
there's a bit of a question mark about whether or not they actually work.

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:17.599
So a lot of them need to be converted back into l-ascorbic acid in your skin before they'll work. The thing I

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:22.480
really like about the Avene formulation is that it's actually been tested to work on skin samples

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:28.480
so it's been found to have the same antioxidant effect as a 15% l-ascorbic acid serum.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:35.439
So on my third night instead of vitamin C a lot of the time now I will use these Bakuchiol Reface pads from indeed labs

